iquid  through a capillary and then applying a  high voltage to it as it passes into the  mass spec source  this creates charged droplets that are  continuously evaporated until the sample  ions are released into the gaseous state  once in this gaseous state the ions can  travel into the inlet of the mass spec  and along the ion path for detection  in apci or atmospheric pressure chemical  ionization however  the sample is vaporizing using a heater  before entering the mass spec source  because the sample is already in the  gaseous state a corona needle is used to  apply an electrical discharge that can  then ionize molecules in the gaseous  state  this allows us to analyze more volatile  compounds while still using lcms  a third ionization source was tested  during the study called dual ionization  or duos this is a compromise between esi  and apci utilizing the esi probe  in combination with the corona needle  discharge  i am going to quickly demonstrate when  using a shimatsu lcms 8060  how to switch from the electrospray  ionization source  to the atmospheric pressure chemical  ionization source or the apci source  the total process of switching from one  source to another takes  less than 30 seconds and can be easily  done by  any user  in the beginning of this study the  initial evaluation included q1 and q3  scans  using electrospray ionization or esi  dual ionization or duos and atmospheric  pressure chemical  ionization or apci every pesticide  currently run by gcms was tested  not only were they run using all these  different ionization techniques  they were actually run using hot and  cold temperature settings  and with and without additives in the  mobile phase all of this initial scan  data was then processed to determine the  best ionization source  and conditions for each pesticide in  this particular example shown  pentachloronitrobenzene or quintazine  showed the best ionization using apci  an in-source rearrangement was seen that  was temperature d